00:00:09.089 --> 00:00:10.089
The Matt Gates story is getting significantly
more interesting and significantly worse for

00:00:10.089 --> 00:00:11.089
Matt Gates to catch you up.

00:00:11.089 --> 00:00:12.660
A Republican congressman from Florida, Matt
Gates, is now in the middle of investigations

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:18.230
into very serious possible crimes, including
child sex trafficking.

00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:23.820
Every time Gates speaks to try to plead his
innocence, he seems to present new derogatory

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:25.500
information about himself.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:31.600
He presents new possible crimes that at least
some of us didn't even know he was under investigation

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:32.600
for.

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:38.260
And we have now learned, thanks to an investigation
from The New York Times, that Matt Gates sought

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:44.890
a preemptive blanket pardon from Donald Trump
at the end of Donald Trump's term.

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:52.860
Now, in retrospect, we know that at the time
that Matt Gates sought this pardon from Donald

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:55.760
Trump, Gates was already under investigation.

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:58.300
We don't know whether Gates knew that.

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:03.879
Was it Gates knowing he was under investigation
that caused him to seek the pardon from Donald

00:01:03.879 --> 00:01:04.879
Trump?

00:01:04.879 --> 00:01:10.079
Or was it Gates knowing he had committed crimes
and wasn't sure whether they would ever be

00:01:10.079 --> 00:01:11.079
investigated?

00:01:11.079 --> 00:01:14.560
That caused him to ask Donald Trump for a
pardon.

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:18.649
The New York Times reports that, quote, in
the final weeks of Trump's term and Gates

00:01:18.649 --> 00:01:23.819
sought something in return for his unending
brownnosing support of Matt Gates.

00:01:23.819 --> 00:01:25.069
That's my of Donald Trump.

00:01:25.069 --> 00:01:26.569
That's my editorializing.

00:01:26.569 --> 00:01:33.359
Gates privately asked the White House for
blanket preemptive pardons for himself and

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:40.340
for unidentified congressional allies for
any crimes they may have committed.

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:41.340
Around this time.

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:48.169
Gates was publicly calling for broad pardons
from Trump to thwart what he termed the, quote,

00:01:48.169 --> 00:01:51.489
bloodlust of their political opponents.

00:01:51.489 --> 00:01:57.279
Justice Department investigators had begun
questioning Gates associates about his conduct,

00:01:57.279 --> 00:02:02.809
including whether he had a sexual relationship
with a 17 year old which violated child sex

00:02:02.809 --> 00:02:09.399
trafficking laws in an inquiry that grew out
of the case of an indicted associate in Florida.

00:02:09.399 --> 00:02:10.700
Now, here's the key line.

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:16.159
As I mentioned, it is unclear whether Gates
or the White House knew at the time that Gates

00:02:16.159 --> 00:02:17.670
was under such an investigation.

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:22.250
It is unclear who else Gates wanted pardons
for.

00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:25.420
He didn't tell the White House he was under
investigation.

00:02:25.420 --> 00:02:29.159
Whether or not he knew it remains a question.

00:02:29.159 --> 00:02:33.769
But according to The New York Times, White
House White House lawyers and officials viewed

00:02:33.769 --> 00:02:41.670
the request for a preemptive pardon as a nonstarter
that would set a bad precedent.

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:49.620
The latest idea is when Gates asked for a
pardon for himself and others, the and others

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:54.829
might have been a way to camouflage his own
criminality.

00:02:54.829 --> 00:03:01.859
In other words, if I know that I have committed
certain crimes or may be under investigation

00:03:01.859 --> 00:03:06.140
for certain crimes, but I don't want to call
attention to that, I could go to Trump and

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:13.560
say, sir, you know, as as he claims people
do myself and a group of my colleagues are

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:18.890
all going to be persecuted for being a supporter
of yours, pardon all of us.

00:03:18.890 --> 00:03:24.459
And you frame it as a preemptive protection
from like political prosecutions, knowing

00:03:24.459 --> 00:03:29.739
that really the reason you want the pardon
is because you may have broken child sex child

00:03:29.739 --> 00:03:34.459
sex trafficking laws and maybe you even know
that you're under investigation.

00:03:34.459 --> 00:03:39.290
It's certainly an idea, and that is what some
Trump associates are speculating went on.

00:03:39.290 --> 00:03:41.430
Now, ultimately, Matt Gates didn't get it.

00:03:41.430 --> 00:03:44.859
As I told you, people around Donald Trump
thought that a preemptive blanket pardon for

00:03:44.859 --> 00:03:47.430
Matt Gates would not be a good look.

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:50.060
And it was not something that Donald Trump
ultimately granted.

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:52.140
So there's a few different layers to this.

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:58.650
Obviously, there's the superficial layer of,
you know, asking for pardons in advance does

00:03:58.650 --> 00:04:00.200
not project innocence.

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:02.510
That's someone with a guilty mind.

00:04:02.510 --> 00:04:04.269
And of course, that's true.

00:04:04.269 --> 00:04:11.319
The counter would be from the right that if
you're anticipating bogus political charges,

00:04:11.319 --> 00:04:15.999
you would look for a blanket pardon as protection,
not because, you know, you committed a crime,

00:04:15.999 --> 00:04:19.699
but because you anticipate that people from
the other political party are going to come

00:04:19.699 --> 00:04:20.699
after you.

00:04:20.699 --> 00:04:23.520
That's just an argument, right?

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:24.520
Both sides.

00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:30.770
A talking point, and it sort of becomes just
an argument about the talking point, the bigger

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:38.360
picture here is it certainly seems as though
Matt Gates must be heading to a massive historic

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:44.110
downfall of epic proportions based on what
continues to be learned every single day.

00:04:44.110 --> 00:04:46.690
You know, he goes on Tucker Carlson to clear
his name.

00:04:46.690 --> 00:04:48.979
He further incriminates himself.

00:04:48.979 --> 00:04:51.970
He says, my travel records will exonerate
me.

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:54.270
They raise even more questions.

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:58.449
Now we learn he was looking for a preemptive
pardon at every opportunity.

00:04:58.449 --> 00:04:59.449
It seems to get worse.

00:04:59.449 --> 00:05:03.669
And logic would point to this guy's got to
be going down, but maybe not.

00:05:03.669 --> 00:05:09.370
Quite frankly, I think it is almost as likely
that this guy has a shot at being a prominent

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:14.210
Republican who knows presidential nominee
with the modern Republican Party.

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:19.470
You can never really tell what they will punish
versus what they will reward.

00:05:19.470 --> 00:05:25.970
And although clearly all signs continue to
point to Gates is in a hell of a massive trouble

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:26.970
here.

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:28.990
How on earth does he get out of this one?

00:05:28.990 --> 00:05:29.990
At the same time?

00:05:29.990 --> 00:05:33.930
This is the Republican Party that we're dealing
with and they are very quick to demand consequences

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:36.810
for those on the left, but not for those on
the right.

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:41.720
This is an area where this is almost like
a critique of the of the Democratic Party,

00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:47.599
sometimes the Democratic Party, in order to
show how they don't care who's doing the wrongdoing.

00:05:47.599 --> 00:05:52.480
The Democratic Party has sometimes been too
quick to demand punishment for those on the

00:05:52.480 --> 00:05:56.580
Democratic side in order to show how not biased
they are.

00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:59.300
Arguably, the Al Franken situation is such
an example.

00:05:59.300 --> 00:06:06.389
So Gates might end up never being heard from
again and resigning in shame or losing reelection,

00:06:06.389 --> 00:06:07.389
going to prison.

00:06:07.389 --> 00:06:08.389
Who the hell knows?

00:06:08.389 --> 00:06:12.639
Or Gates might end up as the vice presidential
nominee in 2024?

00:06:12.639 --> 00:07:19.879
Nothing would surprise me at this point 

00:07:19.879 --> 00:07:22.440
in time.

